Subject: [PATCH 03/46] docs: Flash Next's collectives on a blocking split,
 NCCL_RUNTIME_CONNECT and the measured decode

The two-rank recipe says how start-up stays bounded and what NCCL_RUNTIME_CONNECT=1 would give up; the CUDA recipe's
transport report names Flash Next with GLM; the changelog and the ledger's tensor-parallel row carry the measurements.
